{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"189b78b1-39e2-4281-97bb-1d0f2827048f","step_index":42,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.077993,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"head -n 25 DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/*.md"},"output":"\u003ctruncated 49 lines\u003e\n   - *Selection Status:* **SELECTED** as primary authoritative repository.\r\n2. **Office of the Law Revision Counsel (OLRC) Classification Tables:**\r\n   - *Authority:* U.S. House of Representatives OLRC Table III (*Statutes at Large to U.S. Code*).\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Tabular crosswalk linking public law sections directly to permanent U.S. Code additions.\r\n\r\n==\u003e DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-003.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 003: Phase 3 Administrative Rules and Directives Registry Selection, Authority Querying, and Filter/Citation Schema\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-003.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-002.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nWhat authoritative executive branch rulemaking and administrative directive registries satisfy Phase 3 requirements, how must queries be executed using statutory authority citations (`us_code_citations`), and how are operational filters (`operational_filters`) and clinical citations (`clinical_citations`) extracted?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Datasource Evaluation \u0026 Candidate Selection\r\n\r\n### Evaluated Candidates\r\n1. **Federal Register API (National Archives and Records Administration - NARA):**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official federal rulemaking publication register.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Supports querying documents by statutory authority, CFR title, agency, and full text; provides full preambular narratives, citations, RIN numbers, and regulatory text.\r\n   - *Selection Status:* **SELECTED** as primary authoritative rulemaking API.\r\n2. **Electronic Code of Federal Regulations (eCFR) API (NARA / GPO):**\r\n   - *Authority:* Daily updated codified regulations repository.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Provides point-in-time codified CFR text for 42 CFR Part 410 and Part 414.\r\n\r\n==\u003e DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-004.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 004: Phase 4 Medical Billing, Coverage Determination, and Regional Fee Schedule Schema Reconciliation\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-004.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-003.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nWhat authoritative datasets provide standardized procedure codes, coverage policies, and regional reimbursement fee schedules, how are procedure codes isolated strictly using `operational_filters` without keyword search, and how are diagnostic criteria and regional pricing reconciled into terminal billing entities?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Datasource Evaluation \u0026 Candidate Selection\r\n\r\n### Evaluated Candidates\r\n1. **CMS Alpha-Numeric HCPCS Master Release Files:**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official annual/quarterly alphanumeric HCPCS dataset published by CMS.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Contains all level II healthcare procedure codes with native operational metadata fields (Pricing Indicator, BETOS category, coverage status).\r\n   - *Selection Status:* **SELECTED** as primary master coding repository.\r\n2. **CMS DMEPOS Fee Schedule (Durable Medical Equipment, Prosthetics, Orthotics, and Supplies):**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official CMS state-by-state payment file.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Tabular dataset providing jurisdictional payment allowances, floors, ceilings, and rural/non-rural payment splits for all covered HCPCS items.\r\n\r\n==\u003e DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-005.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 005: Phase 5 Advocacy, Budget Estimates, and Peer-Reviewed Literature Context Integration Schema\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-005.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-001.md`, `ticket-003.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nWhat authoritative repositories provide registered lobbying disclosures, legislative budget estimates, and peer-reviewed literature indexing, and how must parallel queries be executed using `target_bill_ids` and `clinical_citations` to extract advocacy and evidentiary context?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Datasource Evaluation \u0026 Candidate Selection\r\n\r\n### Evaluated Candidates\r\n1. **Lobbying Disclosure Act (LDA) API (U.S. Senate SOPR / House Clerk):**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official statutory lobbying disclosure database governed by 2 U.S.C. Chapter 26.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* REST API indexing registered filers, clients, lobbying issues (e.g., `HCR`), reported expenditures, and specific referenced bills.\r\n   - *Selection Status:* **SELECTED** as authoritative lobbying registry.\r\n2. **Congressional Budget Office (CBO) Cost Estimates Repository:**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official nonpartisan legislative scorekeeping agency for Congress.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Provides formal 10-year budget estimates, direct spending calculations, and hospital cost-offset models indexed by bill number.\r\n\r\n==\u003e DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-006.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 006: Foreign-Key Pipeline Handoff Contracts, Immutable Composite Key Formats, and Lineage Tracking Architecture\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-006.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-001.md`, `ticket-002.md`, `ticket-003.md`, `ticket-004.md`, `ticket-005.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow must foreign-key handoffs be structured, typed, and validated across phases, how are composite primary keys standardized to maintain complete lineage traceability back to originating legislative vehicles, and how must fail-fast termination rules log operational telemetry upon failure?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Immutable Composite Key Standards\r\n\r\nAll entities discovered or passed between pipeline stages must utilize normalized, deterministic composite keys:\r\n\r\n| Entity Type | Composite Identifier Template | Concrete Example | Generation Phase |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **Bill** | `BILL-[congress]-[type]-[number]` | `BILL-117-hr-3630` | Phase 1 |\r\n| **Public Law** | `PLAW-[congress]-[number]` | `PLAW-117-328` | Phase 1 |\r\n| **Statute** | `USC-[title]-[section]-[subsection]` | `USC-42-1395x-s(2)(JJ)` | Phase 2 |\r\n| **Regulation** | `CFR-[title]-[part]-[section]` | `CFR-42-414-214` | Phase 3 |\r\n\r\n==\u003e DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-007.md \u003c==\r\n# Decision Ticket 007: Field Access Matrix, Payload Feasibility Audit, and Dry-Run Verification Specification\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-007.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-006.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow is every target field across all five phases classified into Direct Path (Native Keys) versus Structural Traversal (Derived Keys) with exact selector expressions, and how does the dry-run verification prove unbroken foreign-key traversal from policy keyword to terminal billing and evidentiary records?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Definitive Field Access Matrix\r\n\r\n| Phase | Target Entity / Field | Parent Endpoint / Document | Access Classification | Exact Selector / Extraction Expression | Output Field Type |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **Phase 1** | Candidate Bill Congress | `/v3/bill` | Direct Path | `json.bills[].congress` | `integer` |\r\n| **Phase 1** | Candidate Bill Type | `/v3/bill` | Direct Path | `json.bills[].type` (lowercased) | `string` |\r\n| **Phase 1** | Candidate Bill Number | `/v3/bill` | Direct Path | `json.bills[].number` | `integer` |\r\n| **Phase 1** | Enacted Public Law ID | `/v3/bill/{c}/{t}/{n}` | Direct Path | `json.bill.laws[?(@.type=='Public Law')].number` | `string` (`\"117-328\"`) |\r\n| **Phase 1** | Related Bill Identifiers | `/v3/bill/{c}/{t}/{n}/relatedbills` | Direct Path | `json.relatedBills[].{congress, type, number}` | `array[object]` |\r\n| **Phase 2** | Statutory Amending Section | GovInfo PLAW USLM XML | Structural Traversal | `//section[contains(heading, 'LYMPHEDEMA')]` | XML Node |\r\n"}}}
run_command({"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"head -n 25 DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/*.md"},"output":"<truncated 49 lines>\n   - *Selection Status:* **SELECTED** as primary authoritative repository.\r\n2. **Office of the Law Revision Counsel (OLRC) Classification Tables:**\r\n   - *Authority:* U.S. House of Representatives OLRC Table III (*Statutes at Large to U.S. Code*).\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Tabular crosswalk linking public law sections directly to permanent U.S. Code additions.\r\n\r\n==> DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-003.md <==\r\n# Decision Ticket 003: Phase 3 Administrative Rules and Directives Registry Selection, Authority Querying, and Filter/Citation Schema\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-003.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-002.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nWhat authoritative executive branch rulemaking and administrative directive registries satisfy Phase 3 requirements, how must queries be executed using statutory authority citations (`us_code_citations`), and how are operational filters (`operational_filters`) and clinical citations (`clinical_citations`) extracted?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Datasource Evaluation & Candidate Selection\r\n\r\n### Evaluated Candidates\r\n1. **Federal Register API (National Archives and Records Administration - NARA):**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official federal rulemaking publication register.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Supports querying documents by statutory authority, CFR title, agency, and full text; provides full preambular narratives, citations, RIN numbers, and regulatory text.\r\n   - *Selection Status:* **SELECTED** as primary authoritative rulemaking API.\r\n2. **Electronic Code of Federal Regulations (eCFR) API (NARA / GPO):**\r\n   - *Authority:* Daily updated codified regulations repository.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Provides point-in-time codified CFR text for 42 CFR Part 410 and Part 414.\r\n\r\n==> DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-004.md <==\r\n# Decision Ticket 004: Phase 4 Medical Billing, Coverage Determination, and Regional Fee Schedule Schema Reconciliation\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-004.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-003.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nWhat authoritative datasets provide standardized procedure codes, coverage policies, and regional reimbursement fee schedules, how are procedure codes isolated strictly using `operational_filters` without keyword search, and how are diagnostic criteria and regional pricing reconciled into terminal billing entities?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Datasource Evaluation & Candidate Selection\r\n\r\n### Evaluated Candidates\r\n1. **CMS Alpha-Numeric HCPCS Master Release Files:**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official annual/quarterly alphanumeric HCPCS dataset published by CMS.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Contains all level II healthcare procedure codes with native operational metadata fields (Pricing Indicator, BETOS category, coverage status).\r\n   - *Selection Status:* **SELECTED** as primary master coding repository.\r\n2. **CMS DMEPOS Fee Schedule (Durable Medical Equipment, Prosthetics, Orthotics, and Supplies):**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official CMS state-by-state payment file.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Tabular dataset providing jurisdictional payment allowances, floors, ceilings, and rural/non-rural payment splits for all covered HCPCS items.\r\n\r\n==> DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-005.md <==\r\n# Decision Ticket 005: Phase 5 Advocacy, Budget Estimates, and Peer-Reviewed Literature Context Integration Schema\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-005.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-001.md`, `ticket-003.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nWhat authoritative repositories provide registered lobbying disclosures, legislative budget estimates, and peer-reviewed literature indexing, and how must parallel queries be executed using `target_bill_ids` and `clinical_citations` to extract advocacy and evidentiary context?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Datasource Evaluation & Candidate Selection\r\n\r\n### Evaluated Candidates\r\n1. **Lobbying Disclosure Act (LDA) API (U.S. Senate SOPR / House Clerk):**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official statutory lobbying disclosure database governed by 2 U.S.C. Chapter 26.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* REST API indexing registered filers, clients, lobbying issues (e.g., `HCR`), reported expenditures, and specific referenced bills.\r\n   - *Selection Status:* **SELECTED** as authoritative lobbying registry.\r\n2. **Congressional Budget Office (CBO) Cost Estimates Repository:**\r\n   - *Authority:* Official nonpartisan legislative scorekeeping agency for Congress.\r\n   - *Capabilities:* Provides formal 10-year budget estimates, direct spending calculations, and hospital cost-offset models indexed by bill number.\r\n\r\n==> DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-006.md <==\r\n# Decision Ticket 006: Foreign-Key Pipeline Handoff Contracts, Immutable Composite Key Formats, and Lineage Tracking Architecture\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-006.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-001.md`, `ticket-002.md`, `ticket-003.md`, `ticket-004.md`, `ticket-005.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow must foreign-key handoffs be structured, typed, and validated across phases, how are composite primary keys standardized to maintain complete lineage traceability back to originating legislative vehicles, and how must fail-fast termination rules log operational telemetry upon failure?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Immutable Composite Key Standards\r\n\r\nAll entities discovered or passed between pipeline stages must utilize normalized, deterministic composite keys:\r\n\r\n| Entity Type | Composite Identifier Template | Concrete Example | Generation Phase |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **Bill** | `BILL-[congress]-[type]-[number]` | `BILL-117-hr-3630` | Phase 1 |\r\n| **Public Law** | `PLAW-[congress]-[number]` | `PLAW-117-328` | Phase 1 |\r\n| **Statute** | `USC-[title]-[section]-[subsection]` | `USC-42-1395x-s(2)(JJ)` | Phase 2 |\r\n| **Regulation** | `CFR-[title]-[part]-[section]` | `CFR-42-414-214` | Phase 3 |\r\n\r\n==> DataSources_Agent/wayfinder/20261012T213134-452-7663/tickets/ticket-007.md <==\r\n# Decision Ticket 007: Field Access Matrix, Payload Feasibility Audit, and Dry-Run Verification Specification\r\n\r\n**Ticket ID:** `ticket-007.md`  \r\n**Run ID:** `20261012T213134-452-7663`  \r\n**Status:** RESOLVED  \r\n**Claimed By:** `wayfinder-read-and-plan`  \r\n**Blocked By:** `ticket-006.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Architectural Question\r\nHow is every target field across all five phases classified into Direct Path (Native Keys) versus Structural Traversal (Derived Keys) with exact selector expressions, and how does the dry-run verification prove unbroken foreign-key traversal from policy keyword to terminal billing and evidentiary records?\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Definitive Field Access Matrix\r\n\r\n| Phase | Target Entity / Field | Parent Endpoint / Document | Access Classification | Exact Selector / Extraction Expression | Output Field Type |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| **Phase 1** | Candidate Bill Congress | `/v3/bill` | Direct Path | `json.bills[].congress` | `integer` |\r\n| **Phase 1** | Candidate Bill Type | `/v3/bill` | Direct Path | `json.bills[].type` (lowercased) | `string` |\r\n| **Phase 1** | Candidate Bill Number | `/v3/bill` | Direct Path | `json.bills[].number` | `integer` |\r\n| **Phase 1** | Enacted Public Law ID | `/v3/bill/{c}/{t}/{n}` | Direct Path | `json.bill.laws[?(@.type=='Public Law')].number` | `string` (`\"117-328\"`) |\r\n| **Phase 1** | Related Bill Identifiers | `/v3/bill/{c}/{t}/{n}/relatedbills` | Direct Path | `json.relatedBills[].{congress, type, number}` | `array[object]` |\r\n| **Phase 2** | Statutory Amending Section | GovInfo PLAW USLM XML | Structural Traversal | `//section[contains(heading, 'LYMPHEDEMA')]` | XML Node |\r\n"})
